From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0470: AMD's signed FSR runtime for temporal_aa=fsr on Direct3D 12: FSR 4.1 (ML) on the Radeon 880M, FSR 3.1.6 fallback

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (S6, from the S5 report $WORK/scratch/S5/REPORT.md). The calls are the public
  FidelityFX SDK 2.4.0 ffx-api (MIT): ffxQueryDescGetVersions, ffxOverrideVersion, ffxQueryGetProviderVersion and
  ffxCreateContextDescUpscaleVersion (type and struct as in ffx_upscale.h of that tag); nothing is taken from LARecomp
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause). The two DLLs
  it fetches are AMD's signed FidelityFX SDK 2.4.0 binaries, listed under the MIT licence in that tag's docs/license.md
  (fetched at configure time and never vendored; the licence is installed next to them)
Purpose: temporal_aa=fsr runs FSR 4.1.2 (the machine-learning upscaler; the Radeon 800M series has its INT8 model since
  FidelityFX SDK 2.4) instead of FSR 3.1.4 when AMD's signed runtime (amd_fidelityfx_loader_dx12.dll +
  amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_dx12.dll) is next to the executable; the same inputs and the same ffx-api calls. Cvar
  temporal_aa_upscaler (GPU, string, auto|fsr3|fsr4, default auto, hot reload: the upscaler is made again) and the
  transient temporal_aa_upscaler_active ("FSR 4.1.2", "FSR 3.1.6", "FSR 3.1.4 (built)", "none"). Log line `Temporal AA:
  FSR 4.1.2 ready for 1920x1080 from 960x540 (Direct3D 12) after N ms` (the real version, from
  ffxQueryGetProviderVersion). FSR 4 needs no reactive mask: its snapshots are not made. A failed FSR 4 context is made
  again pinned to FSR 3.1.6; without the signed DLLs the FSR 3.1.4 built from source runs as before (frame generation and
  Vulkan are untouched). cmake: REXGLUE_FSR_SIGNED (ON), REXGLUE_FSR_SIGNED_DIR. Windows with D3D12 only. Not built before
  the next SDK build.
Bucket: REDO

0470-fsr4-signed-upscaler.patch (mcla-x86 S6; design and licence check in $WORK/scratch/S5/REPORT.md, probe in $WORK/scratch/S6/probe)

Change.
  * cmake/rexglue_fsr_signed.cmake (new; included after rexglue_fsr.cmake): when WIN32, REXGLUE_ENABLE_FSR and D3D12 are on
    (option REXGLUE_FSR_SIGNED, ON) it fetches, from the commit of the v2.4.0 tag of GPUOpen-LibrariesAndSDKs/FidelityFX-SDK
    (7539ae8b6568ad29ed78a753404351daf3b5cca7, raw.githubusercontent.com), Kits/FidelityFX/signedbin/
    amd_fidelityfx_loader_dx12.dll (SHA-256 e2191d3c0828be45eb8affd4e3ec0378f2293adc345b772a7170edcf3b021ecb, 39,184 bytes),
    amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_dx12.dll (aad4fccccb29084a655f9a4f9f613bd22c8c03fb4a0f8840148cc6543b4ccace, 57,664,272 bytes)
    and docs/license.md (410f9c138e766e846acf2dc93db768198def0293a017d7e3296815b451688dbe), checks each against its SHA-256
    (through a temporary name, renamed only once verified) and installs the DLLs to bin/ and the licence as
    bin/amd_fidelityfx_signed_LICENSE.md. REXGLUE_FSR_SIGNED_DIR (cache path) may name a folder that already holds the
    three files. A file that cannot be fetched or verified is a warning, not an error: the SDK builds without them and the
    GPU plugin runs the FSR 3.1.4 it built. The configure summary gains `FSR (signed runtime): ...`.
  * src/graphics/temporal_aa_fsr.h: the 2.x create-description type (0x0001000B) and FFX_UPSCALER_VERSION (4.1.2), defined
    here rather than by bumping the 1.1.4 headers the Vulkan backend and frame generation use; FsrRuntime::Load(api,
    signed_loader = false) and signed_loader(); FsrUpscalerVersion, FsrListUpscalerVersions (ffxQueryDescGetVersions:
    count, then ids and names together, names copied), FsrPickUpscalerVersion (the newest of fsr4 = 4.x / fsr3 = 3.x), FsrLabel.
  * src/graphics/temporal_aa.cpp: the two cvars; Load tries amd_fidelityfx_loader_dx12.dll when
    amd_fidelityfx_upscaler_dx12.dll is beside it, and falls back to amd_fidelityfx_dx12.dll (so every caller of
    Load("vk") and the PS5 static link behave as before); the helpers above.
  * src/graphics/d3d12/temporal_aa.cpp: Load("dx12", true); on the context thread the chain is create -> version
    (signed runtime only) -> ffxOverrideVersion (only when fsr3/fsr4 pins one; fsr4 without an FSR 4 offered warns and pins
    FSR 3) -> backend; the offered versions are logged; a failed create is tried once more pinned to FSR 3; the ready line
    carries the version the runtime reports; temporal_aa_upscaler_active is published on the submission thread when the
    context is first used and reset to none on release; a changed temporal_aa_upscaler releases the context at the end of
    the frame (the size-change path); TaaSnapshot returns false with an FSR 4 provider (no luminance snapshots, no
    reactive mask: temporal_aa_reactive is ignored); TaaCheckAvailable accepts the loader pair or the built DLL.

Evidence (probe $WORK/scratch/S6/probe/probe.exe, a D3D12 device on the Radeon 880M, driver 32.0.32029.2010, Windows 11
24H2, in-box D3D12 (no Agility SDK), the pinned DLLs next to it):
  * CheckFeatureSupport(D3D12_FEATURE_SHADER_MODEL) answers highest 6_9: SM 6.6 (FSR 4's CS_6_6) is there.
  * ffxQuery(GET_VERSIONS, upscaler) -> 3 versions, names "4.1.2", "3.1.6", "2.3.4" (no "FSR " prefix), ids
    0xF5A5CA1E01001002 / 0xF5A5CA1E00C01006 / 0xF5A5CA1E00803004 (low 32 bits = (major<<22)|(minor<<12)|patch).
  * No override -> provider "4.1.2" (context made in ~140 ms); pinned: 4.1.2, 3.1.6 (~0.9 s), 2.3.4 all create.
  * One dispatch 960x540 -> 1920x1080 on zeroed inputs, RCAS 0.2, GPU timestamps, 120 runs after 20 warm-up, three
    runs: FSR 4.1.2 median 3.48 / 3.69 / 3.60 ms (min 3.25-3.53, p95 3.6-4.3); FSR 3.1.6 median 1.79 / 1.95 ms; FSR 2.3.4
    1.80 ms. (S5 had estimated 3.2-3.4 ms for FSR 4; the probe is idle-GPU and static content, the game's pass may differ.)
Checked: the cmake fetch, hash mismatch (soft failure), the REXGLUE_FSR_SIGNED_DIR path and the install step in a small
project; the scratch tree configures (summary `FSR (signed runtime): ON (...)`); clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only with the SDK's
Release flags on src/graphics/temporal_aa.cpp, d3d12/temporal_aa.cpp, vulkan/temporal_aa.cpp and vulkan/frame_generation.cpp:
no new diagnostics. Not run in the game.
